      <div type="clause" n="15.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 15.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>E s’il aver nes pot, aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.f"/> a la juise a treis duble, si cum il deust a treis duble serment.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>E s’il aveir<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.24"/> nes pot, aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.25"/> a la juise a treis dublez<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.26"/>, si co[m]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.27"/> il doust a treis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.28"/> dublein serment.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>Si eos habere non potest, eat ad iudicium triplex, si[cut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.2"/>] iuramentum debuit exhiberi triplex.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="15.2" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="260" ed="#robertson"/>E s'il aver nes pot, aut a la juise a treis duble, si cum il deust a treis duble serment.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="502–503" ed="#liebermann"/>15, 2. Und wenn er diese [36] nicht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.de1.b"/> erlangen kann, schreite er zum dreidoppelten [Eisen]ordal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_15-2.lnote.de1.d"/>, so wie er hätte zum dreidoppelten Eide [schreiten] sollen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">15, 2. And if he cannot obtain these [36], he shall proceed to the threefold [iron] ordeal, just as he should have [proceeded] to the threefold oath.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="261" ed="#robertson"/>And if he cannot find them, he shall go to the triple ordeal, just as he had [to produce] a triple oath.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 502–503, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">alt <hi rend="italic">bessert BA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">alt emended by BA.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">auer <hi rend="italic">Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">auer <hi rend="italic">Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dubles <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dubles <hi rend="italic">Io Isp</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">co <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">co <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">502</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tris <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tris <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">S Edd.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si <hi rend="italic">S edd.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">zur Eideshilfe willig</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">willing to act as oath-helpers</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.de1.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">503</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iudicium <hi rend="italic">im engen Sinne auch</hi> Wl episc. 4, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iudicium in the narrow sense also Wl episc. 4, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_15-2.lnote.de._" n="-" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">288</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eisenordal 1. 8; Beweis 8e ff.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eisenordal 1. 8; Beweis 8e ff.</seg></note>
      </div>
